  <h2>Who can use Strong Hire</h2>
  <p>You must be 18 or older and live in the United States or Canada. One account per person.</p>

  <h2>What Strong Hire is</h2>
  <p>
    Strong Hire is interview practice. An AI interviewer asks questions and an AI scorer gives feedback. The hire signal
    and scores are practice estimates. They are not a prediction of any company's hiring decision, and they are not
    career, legal or employment advice.
  </p>
  <p>{NOT_AFFILIATED} Descriptions of how a company interviews come from public sources and are written in our own words.</p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    Your CV, job postings and answers stay yours. You give us permission to process them only to run the service for you.
    Upload only content you have the right to use. Don't share questions from interviews you agreed to keep confidential.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Don't use Strong Hire during a real interview, or to impersonate someone else.</li>
    <li>Don't try to break, overload or reverse engineer the service, or to get the AI to produce harmful content.</li>
    <li>Don't resell access.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Plans and minutes</h2>
  <p>
    Paid plans, prices and the refund policy are shown before you pay. Minutes are counted while an interview runs. See
    <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> and <a href="/legal/refunds">refunds</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    During the beta, features can change and the service can be interrupted. We may update these terms; we will tell you
    by email before changes that affect you take effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account at any time from the Account page. We may suspend an account that breaks these terms, and
    will tell you why.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</p>
</Legal>
